,'',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/glow-70mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(121,0,'2026-03-12 20:17:41','2026-03-12 08:17:41','','Mots C 10mg','','inherit','open','closed','','mots-c-10mg','','','2026-03-12 20:17:41','2026-03-12 08:17:41','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/mots-c-10mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(122,0,'2026-03-12 20:17:52','2026-03-12 08:17:52','','Nad Plus 500mg','','inherit','open','closed','','nad-plus-500mg','','','2026-03-12 20:17:52','2026-03-12 08:17:52','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/nad-plus-500mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(123,0,'2026-03-12 20:18:05','2026-03-12 08:18:05','','Retatrutide 10mg','','inherit','open','closed','','retatrutide-10mg','','','2026-03-12 20:18:05','2026-03-12 08:18:05','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/retatrutide-10mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(124,0,'2026-03-12 20:18:20','2026-03-12 08:18:20','','Selank 10mg','','inherit','open','closed','','selank-10mg','','','2026-03-12 20:18:20','2026-03-12 08:18:20','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/selank-10mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(125,0,'2026-03-12 20:18:32','2026-03-12 08:18:32','','Semax 10mg 2','','inherit','open','closed','','semax-10mg-2','','','2026-03-12 20:18:32','2026-03-12 08:18:32','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/semax-10mg-2.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(126,0,'2026-03-12 20:18:46','2026-03-12 08:18:46','','Semax 10mg','','inherit','open','closed','','semax-10mg','','','2026-03-12 20:18:46','2026-03-12 08:18:46','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/semax-10mg.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(127,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:17','2026-03-12 10:48:17','<p>BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound 157) is a synthetic pentadecapeptide derived from a gastric protective protein, studied extensively in preclinical tissue and connective structure research.</p>\n<p>Published studies have examined BPC-157 in models relating to gastrointestinal mucosal integrity, tendon and ligament structure, and skeletal muscle tissue. The peer-reviewed literature explores its interaction with nitric oxide pathways, VEGF expression, and collagen organisation at sites of experimental tissue disruption. Researchers have also investigated its interactions with dopaminergic and serotonergic systems in central nervous system models.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','BPC-157 10mg','BPC-157 (Body Protective Compound) 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','bpc-157-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:28','2026-04-06 13:12:28','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/bpc-157-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(128,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:22','2026-03-12 10:48:22','<p>This combination vial contains BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound 157) and TB-500 (Thymosin Beta-4), two peptides studied independently and together in preclinical connective tissue and cytoskeletal research.</p>\n<p>BPC-157 has been explored for its interactions with nitric oxide pathways, fibroblast behaviour, and collagen organisation. TB-500 is studied as a G-actin sequestering peptide influencing cell migration, differentiation, and angiogenesis. Researchers have noted the compounds operate via largely distinct molecular pathways, and preclinical literature has explored whether complementary mechanisms produce additive effects. The 5mg + 5mg ratio reflects the most common split documented in published combination protocols.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> BPC-157 5mg + TB-500 5mg (10mg total), co-lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','BPC-157 + TB-500 5mg + 5mg','BPC-157 + TB-500 blend, 5mg + 5mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','bpc-157-tb-500-5mg-5mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:29','2026-04-06 13:12:29','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/bpc-157-tb-500-5mg-5mg/',0,'product','',0),(129,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:28','2026-03-12 10:48:28','<p>CJC-1295 No DAC (Mod GRF 1-29) is a stabilised synthetic analogue of growth hormone-releasing hormone (GHRH), representing the biologically active 1-29 fragment with four amino acid substitutions that improve stability, studied in growth hormone secretagogue research.</p>\n<p>The peer-reviewed literature characterises it as a GHRH receptor agonist that stimulates pituitary somatotroph cells in preclinical models. Unlike its DAC-conjugated counterpart, the No DAC form exhibits a shorter half-life approximating endogenous GHRH, useful for studying temporal dynamics of GH secretion. The modification pattern confers resistance to dipeptidyl peptidase-IV cleavage while preserving receptor binding affinity. Researchers have examined it in combination with ghrelin-mimetic peptides for dual-pathway somatotropic axis studies.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','CJC-1295 NO DAC 10mg','CJC-1295 without DAC, 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','cjc-1295-no-dac-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:31','2026-04-06 13:12:31','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/cjc-1295-no-dac-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(130,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:33','2026-03-12 10:48:33','<p>This combination vial contains CJC-1295 No DAC (Mod GRF 1-29), a stabilised GHRH analogue, and Ipamorelin, a selective pentapeptide growth hormone secretagogue, studied in preclinical somatotropic axis research.</p>\n<p>CJC-1295 No DAC acts as a GHRH receptor agonist stimulating pulsatile pituitary GH release. Ipamorelin operates via the ghrelin receptor (GHS-R1a) through a distinct pathway; published studies report minimal co-stimulation of ACTH and cortisol compared with earlier-generation GH secretagogues. Preclinical literature documents that dual-pathway agonism produces a synergistic effect on GH pulse amplitude. The 5mg + 5mg equimolar split reflects the ratio most commonly reported in published combination protocols.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> CJC-1295 No DAC 5mg + Ipamorelin 5mg (10mg total), co-lyophilised</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','CJC-1295 NO DAC + Ipamorelin 5mg + 5mg','CJC-1295 NO DAC + Ipamorelin blend, 5mg + 5mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','cjc-1295-no-dac-ipamorelin-5mg-5mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:34','2026-04-06 13:12:34','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/cjc-1295-no-dac-ipamorelin-5mg-5mg/',0,'product','',0),(131,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:39','2026-03-12 10:48:39','<p>CJC-1295 with DAC is a synthetic GHRH analogue conjugated to a Drug Affinity Complex (DAC) via a reactive maleimide group that forms a covalent bond with serum albumin, studied in sustained-release GH secretagogue research.</p>\n<p>Published pharmacokinetic studies document a markedly prolonged plasma half-life of several days in rodent and primate models, attributed to the DAC moiety protecting the peptide from proteolytic degradation and renal clearance. Researchers have investigated sustained elevations in GH and IGF-1 levels in preclinical settings. The compound serves as a useful comparator in studies examining biological consequences of sustained GH baseline elevation versus pulsatile GH release patterns.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 5mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','CJC-1295 WITH DAC 5mg','CJC-1295 with DAC, 5mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','cjc-1295-with-dac-5mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:32','2026-04-06 13:12:32','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/cjc-1295-with-dac-5mg/',0,'product','',0),(132,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:45','2026-03-12 10:48:45','<p>GHK-Cu (glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine copper complex) is a naturally occurring tripeptide-copper complex first isolated from human plasma, investigated extensively in wound biology, dermatological research, and cellular senescence studies.</p>\n<p>Published studies have identified GHK-Cu\'s role in upregulating collagen, elastin, and glycosaminoglycan synthesis in fibroblast cultures, and its modulation of matrix metalloproteinase activity in extracellular matrix remodelling. Researchers have characterised its interactions with the ubiquitin-proteasome pathway and its capacity to modulate pro-inflammatory cytokine signalling in macrophage models. Antioxidant defence pathway activation, including superoxide dismutase and catalase expression, has also been documented in the peer-reviewed literature.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 100mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','GHK-Cu 100mg','Copper Peptide GHK-Cu, 100mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','ghk-cu-100mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:42','2026-04-06 13:12:42','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/ghk-cu-100mg/',0,'product','',0),(133,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:51','2026-03-12 10:48:51','<p>Glow 70mg is a copper peptide research blend formulated around GHK-Cu (glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine copper complex), studied in dermal biology and extracellular matrix research, designed for investigators examining combined copper-binding peptide activity in skin-analogous tissue models.</p>\n<p>GHK-Cu has been investigated for its role in regulating collagen, elastin, and glycosaminoglycan synthesis in fibroblast cultures, modulating matrix metalloproteinase activity, and influencing antioxidant enzyme expression. Research into copper peptide blends examines whether adjunct compounds can potentiate or modulate GHK-Cu\'s documented activity profile in vitro. This concentrated vial format suits extended in vitro protocol series without requiring repeated reconstitution from individual components.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 70mg lyophilised powder (GHK-Cu blend)</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','Glow 70mg','Glow peptide blend, 70mg vial. Research use only.','draft','open','closed','','glow-70mg','','','2026-04-06 18:57:23','2026-04-06 06:57:23','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/glow-70mg/',0,'product','',0),(134,1,'2026-03-12 22:48:56','2026-03-12 10:48:56','<p>MOTS-c (Mitochondrial Open Reading Frame of the 12S rRNA-c) is a 16-amino-acid peptide encoded within the mitochondrial 12S rRNA gene, investigated as a mitochondria-derived peptide in cellular metabolism, insulin sensitivity signalling, and mitochondrial function research.</p>\n<p>The peer-reviewed literature identifies MOTS-c as a regulator of the folate-methionine cycle and a modulator of AMPK signalling. Published studies have documented its translocation to the nucleus under metabolic stress, where it interacts with antioxidant response element promoter regions. Researchers have examined its effects on glucose utilisation and fatty acid oxidation in skeletal muscle cell models. Preclinical literature has also explored MOTS-c in the context of mitohormesis, with documented changes in metabolic biomarkers in ageing rodent models.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','MOTS-c 10mg','MOTS-c mitochondrial peptide, 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','mots-c-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:38','2026-04-06 13:12:38','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/mots-c-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(135,1,'2026-03-12 22:49:02','2026-03-12 10:49:02','<p>NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is a coenzyme found in all living cells, functioning as a critical cofactor in oxidation-reduction reactions, investigated extensively in mitochondrial function, DNA repair, and cellular senescence biology.</p>\n<p>The published literature characterises NAD+ as an essential substrate for sirtuins (SIRT1-7), poly(ADP-ribose) polymerases (PARPs), and CD38. Researchers have investigated how NAD+ availability influences sirtuin-mediated deacetylation and downstream effects on mitochondrial biogenesis and autophagy. Preclinical longevity literature has examined NAD+ restoration in aged animal models, documenting changes in mitochondrial respiratory function. NAD+ is hygroscopic and sensitive to freeze-thaw cycling; researchers should plan reconstitution protocols accordingly.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 500mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','NAD+ 500mg','NAD+ (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide), 500mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','nad-500mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:39','2026-04-06 13:12:39','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/nad-500mg/',0,'product','',0),(136,1,'2026-03-12 22:49:07','2026-03-12 10:49:07','<p>Retatrutide is a synthetic acylated peptide acting as a triple agonist at the GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R), glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide receptor (GIPR), and glucagon receptor (GCGR), distinguishing it from dual and single agonist peptides in current metabolic research.</p>\n<p>GLP-1R agonism promotes glucose-dependent insulin secretion and central satiety signalling; GIPR agonism has been investigated for additive effects on insulin secretion and adipocyte signalling. GCGR agonism has been studied for hepatic glucose output and thermogenic signalling in brown adipose tissue models. Phase 2 clinical data characterises its extended half-life attributable to C18 fatty acid acylation and albumin binding, enabling once-weekly dosing in clinical research contexts.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','Retatrutide 10mg','Retatrutide triple agonist peptide, 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','retatrutide-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:26','2026-04-06 13:12:26','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/retatrutide-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(137,1,'2026-03-12 22:49:12','2026-03-12 10:49:12','<p>Selank is a synthetic heptapeptide (Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro) derived from the endogenous immunomodulatory peptide tuftsin, with a stabilising Pro-Gly-Pro sequence, investigated primarily in anxiolytic-adjacent behavioural neuroscience and cognitive research.</p>\n<p>Published studies characterise Selank\'s interaction with the GABAergic system, examining GABA receptor complex modulation and its downstream effects on anxiety-related behaviour in rodent models. The literature documents its inhibition of enkephalin-degrading enzymes, proposed as a mechanism influencing endogenous opioid peptide activity. Researchers have also investigated changes in BDNF levels in rodent hippocampal tissue, serotonin and dopamine turnover, and immunomodulatory properties including effects on interleukin profiles and T-lymphocyte activity consistent with its structural relationship to tuftsin.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','Selank 10mg','Selank nootropic peptide, 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','selank-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:36','2026-04-06 13:12:36','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/selank-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(138,1,'2026-03-12 22:49:18','2026-03-12 10:49:18','<p>Semax is a synthetic heptapeptide analogue of the ACTH 4-7 fragment (Met-Glu-His-Phe-Pro-Gly-Pro), modified with a Pro-Gly-Pro sequence for enzymatic resistance, investigated in neuroprotection, cognitive function, and neurotrophic factor signalling research.</p>\n<p>The peer-reviewed literature characterises Semax as a potent modulator of BDNF expression, with rodent studies documenting substantial increases in BDNF mRNA and protein in the hippocampus and cerebral cortex. Researchers have also explored its effects on VEGF and NGF expression. A significant body of published work has investigated Semax in ischaemia-related research models, examining oxidative stress markers, neuroinflammatory signalling, and neuronal survival parameters following experimental oxygen-glucose deprivation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Amount per vial:</strong> 10mg lyophilised powder</li>\n<li>Lyophilised powder; reconstitute with bacteriostatic water</li>\n<li>Store at -20°C pre-reconstitution; 2-8°C post-reconstitution; use within 28 days</li>\n<li>Third-party tested by Janoshik Analytical (min. purity 98%+)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For laboratory research use only.</p>','Semax 10mg','Semax nootropic peptide, 10mg vial. Research use only.','publish','open','closed','','semax-10mg','','','2026-04-07 01:12:35','2026-04-06 13:12:35','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/semax-10mg/',0,'product','',0),(139,1,'2026-03-12 22:49:23','2026-03-12 10:49:23','<p>Bacteriostatic water is sterile water for injection preserved with 0.9% benzyl alcohol (9mg/mL), the standard reconstitution solvent for lyophilised peptide compounds in research settings requiring multi-draw vial access.</p>\n<p>Benzyl alcohol inhibits the growth of most common bacteria, allowing repeated re-entry of the vial without compromising sterility. This is particularly relevant for peptides reconstituted at low concentrations drawn across multiple experimental sessions. Researchers should confirm benzyl alcohol compatibility with the target peptide before use, as it is not suitable in contexts where the preservative may interact with the compound under investigation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Volume per vial:</strong> 10mL multi-dose vial</li>\n<li><strong>Preservative:</strong> 0.9% benzyl alcohol (9mg/mL)</li>\n<li>Store at room temperature or 2-8°C; do not freeze</li>\n<li>Refrigerate after first draw; use within 28 days of opening</li>\n<li>Do not use past expiry, if seal integrity is compromised, or if solution appears discoloured or cloudy</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Supplied by Eterna Peptides as a laboratory research supply item.</p>','Bacteriostatic Water 10mL','Bacteriostatic Water, 0.9% Benzyl Alcohol, 10mL sterile vial.','publish','open','closed','','bacteriostatic-water-10ml','','','2026-04-07 01:12:43','2026-04-06 13:12:43','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product/bacteriostatic-water-10ml/',0,'product','',0),(140,1,'2026-03-13 00:06:45','2026-03-12 12:06:45','','Untitled design (9)','','inherit','open','closed','','untitled-design-9','','','2026-03-13 00:06:45','2026-03-12 12:06:45','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Untitled-design-9.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(141,1,'2026-03-13 00:06:49','2026-03-12 12:06:49','','Untitled design (8)','','inherit','open','closed','','untitled-design-8','','','2026-03-13 00:06:49','2026-03-12 12:06:49','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Untitled-design-8.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(142,1,'2026-03-13 