ty.</p>                \n                <h4>(04)</h4> Volume Discounts \n                    <p>Save 10% on 2+ items and 15% on 3+ items — applied automatically at checkout. No codes needed.</p>                \n					<h4>Step 01</h4>					<h3>Sourced</h3>		<p>From GMP-certified facilities with strict quality controls</p>			<h4>Step 02</h4>					<h3>Tested</h3>		<p>Independent HPLC and mass spectrometry verification</p>			<h4>Step 03</h4>					<h3>Delivered\n</h3>		<p>Cold-chain shipped with tracked courier across NZ</p>			<h2>Ready to explore our range?</h2>		<p>Browse our full catalogue of research-grade peptides and accessories.</p>								<a href=\"https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/shop/\">\n									Shop\n					</a>','About Eterna Labs','','inherit','closed','closed','','232-revision-v1','','','2026-03-13 10:55:28','2026-03-12 22:55:28','',232,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/?p=328',0,'revision','',0),(329,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:01','2026-03-12 23:13:01','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Research peptides are generating serious interest across the scientific community — but what exactly are they, and why are researchers paying attention?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Peptides 101</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peptides are short chains of amino acids, typically ranging from 2 to 50 amino acids in length. They\'re essentially smaller versions of proteins, and they play critical roles in nearly every biological process — from tissue repair and immune response to hormone regulation and cognitive function.<br>Unlike full proteins, peptides are small enough to be synthesised in a lab with high precision, making them valuable tools for research into specific biological pathways.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What makes a peptide \"research-grade\"?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not all peptides are created equal. Research-grade peptides are manufactured to strict purity standards — typically 98% or higher — and are verified through independent testing methods like HPLC (High-Performance Liquid Chromatography) and mass spectrometry.<br>At Eterna Labs, every batch comes with the option to request a Certificate of Analysis (COA) confirming purity and identity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common categories of research peptides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peptides are often grouped by their area of biological activity:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Recovery peptides</strong> — such as BPC-157 and TB-500, studied for their role in tissue repair and healing processes</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Growth hormone peptides</strong> — including CJC-1295 and Ipamorelin, researched for their effects on growth hormone secretion</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Neuropeptides</strong> — like Semax and Selank, investigated for cognitive and neuroprotective properties</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Longevity peptides</strong> — such as NAD+ and MOTS-c, explored for their role in cellular energy and ageing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Skin peptides</strong> — including GHK-Cu, studied for skin regeneration and wound healing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How are research peptides used?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Research peptides are used exclusively in laboratory and research settings. They are not intended for human consumption. Researchers use them to study biological mechanisms, test hypotheses about cellular processes, and explore potential therapeutic pathways.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Proper handling matters</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peptides are sensitive compounds. Most are supplied in lyophilised (freeze-dried) form and need to be reconstituted with bacteriostatic water before use in research. Proper storage — refrigerated at 2-8°C, away from light — is essential to maintain stability and integrity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why source matters</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The peptide market varies widely in quality. Sourcing from a supplier that provides third-party tested, GMP-sourced peptides ensures your research starts with reliable, verified compounds. That\'s exactly what Eterna Labs delivers — every vial, every time.</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade peptides across New Zealand. Browse our full range at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— one of the most widely researched peptides; used as an introductory example</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/selank-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Selank</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a nootropic peptide referenced to illustrate cognitive research applications</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/retatrutide-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Retatrutide</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a newer compound cited to show how peptide research is evolving</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','What Are Research Peptides? A Beginner\'s Guide','','publish','open','open','','what-are-research-peptides','','','2026-04-06 03:20:05','2026-04-05 15:20:05','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/what-are-research-peptides/',0,'post','',0),(330,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:04','2026-03-12 23:13:04','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>BPC-157 is one of the most widely studied peptides in the recovery and tissue repair space. Here\'s what the research tells us.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is BPC-157?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound-157) is a synthetic peptide derived from a naturally occurring protein found in human gastric juice. It consists of 15 amino acids and has been the subject of numerous preclinical studies exploring its regenerative properties.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What does the research show?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The bulk of BPC-157 research has been conducted in animal models. Key areas of study include:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tissue repair and healing</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Multiple studies have demonstrated BPC-157\'s potential to accelerate healing in tendons, ligaments, muscles, and the gastrointestinal tract. Research suggests it may promote angiogenesis (the formation of new blood vessels), which is critical for tissue repair.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Gut health</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Given its origin in gastric juice, BPC-157 has been extensively studied for its effects on the gastrointestinal system. Animal studies have shown protective effects against various forms of gut damage, including ulcers and inflammatory conditions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Neuroprotective effects</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Emerging research suggests BPC-157 may have neuroprotective properties, with studies exploring its effects on dopaminergic and serotonergic pathways.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bone and joint healing</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Preclinical studies have investigated BPC-157\'s effects on bone healing and joint recovery, with promising results in fracture repair models.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">BPC-157 vs BPC-157 + TB-500</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Some researchers choose to study BPC-157 alongside TB-500 (Thymosin Beta-4), another peptide associated with tissue repair. The two peptides are thought to work through complementary mechanisms — BPC-157 primarily through angiogenesis and growth factor modulation, and TB-500 through actin regulation and cell migration.<br>Eterna Labs offers both <a href=\"/shop/\">BPC-157 10mg</a> and <a href=\"/shop/\">BPC-157 + TB-500 5mg + 5mg</a> for researchers who want to study either compound individually or in combination.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Handling and storage</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>BPC-157 is supplied as a lyophilised powder. For research use:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Reconstitution:</strong> Use bacteriostatic water</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Storage:</strong> Refrigerate at 2-8°C</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Stability:</strong> Use reconstituted peptide within 30 days</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Protection:</strong> Keep away from direct sunlight and heat</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Purity matters</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">BPC-157\'s biological activity is highly dependent on peptide purity. Low-quality sources may contain impurities that interfere with research outcomes. All Eterna Labs BPC-157 is independently tested to a minimum of 98% purity via HPLC analysis.</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade BPC-157 across New Zealand. View our recovery peptides at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the primary research compound covered throughout this article</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-tb-500-5mg-5mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157 + TB-500</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a popular combination protocol studied for synergistic regenerative effects</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','BPC-157: What Researchers Need to Know','','publish','open','open','','bpc-157-what-researchers-need-to-know','','','2026-04-06 03:20:00','2026-04-05 15:20:00','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/bpc-157-what-researchers-need-to-know/',0,'post','',0),(331,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:05','2026-03-12 23:13:05','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Proper storage and reconstitution are essential for maintaining peptide integrity in research settings. Here\'s a straightforward guide.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why storage matters</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peptides are biological molecules that degrade when exposed to heat, moisture, light, and bacterial contamination. Incorrect storage can reduce purity, alter structure, and compromise research results. A few simple precautions go a long way.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Storing lyophilised (freeze-dried) peptides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most research peptides are supplied in lyophilised form — a dry, stable powder. In this state, they\'re relatively hardy, but still need proper care:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Short-term (up to 30 days):</strong> Refrigerate at 2-8°C</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Long-term (1-12 months):</strong> Store at -20°C in a freezer</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Extended storage (12+ months):</strong> Store at -80°C for maximum stability</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Always:</strong> Keep in a sealed container away from direct sunlight and moisture<br>Most researchers will be fine storing lyophilised peptides in a standard fridge or freezer.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Reconstituting peptides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Reconstitution is the process of dissolving the lyophilised powder into a liquid solution for research use. The standard solvent is bacteriostatic water (BAC water).</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step-by-step process</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Allow the peptide vial to reach room temperature</strong> — removing a cold vial and immediately adding liquid can cause condensation and degradation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Draw up the appropriate volume of bacteriostatic water</strong> using a sterile syringe</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Inject the water slowly down the inside wall of the vial</strong> — never spray directly onto the powder, as this can damage the peptide</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Swirl gently</strong> to dissolve — do not shake vigorously, as this can denature the peptide</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Wait until fully dissolved</strong> — the solution should be clear with no visible particles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How much BAC water to use</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The volume depends on your desired concentration. A common approach:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>2mL BAC water into a 10mg vial</strong> = 5mg/mL concentration</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>1mL BAC water into a 5mg vial</strong> = 5mg/mL concentration<br>Adjust based on your specific research requirements.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Storing reconstituted peptides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once reconstituted, peptides are less stable than in lyophilised form:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Refrigerate at 2-8°C immediately</strong> after reconstitution</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Use within 30 days</strong> for best results</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Do not freeze</strong> reconstituted peptides — the freeze-thaw cycle can damage the molecular structure</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Use sterile technique</strong> every time you draw from the vial to prevent bacterial contamination</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is bacteriostatic water?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Bacteriostatic water is sterile water containing 0.9% benzyl alcohol, which prevents bacterial growth. This makes it the preferred solvent for reconstituting peptides, as it allows for multiple draws from the same vial over time without contamination risk.<br>Eterna Labs stocks <a href=\"/shop/\">Bacteriostatic Water 10mL</a> specifically for this purpose.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common mistakes to avoid</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Shaking the vial</strong> — always swirl gently</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Using regular sterile water</strong> — it lacks the preservative needed for multi-use vials</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Leaving reconstituted peptides at room temperature</strong> — refrigerate immediately</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Freezing reconstituted peptides</strong> — stick to refrigeration only</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">- <strong>Using a contaminated syringe</strong> — always use fresh, sterile equipment</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade peptides and bacteriostatic water across New Zealand. Shop at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bacteriostatic-water-10ml\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Bacteriostatic Water</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the recommended reconstitution solvent covered in this guide</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-tb-500-5mg-5mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157 + TB-500</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a commonly reconstituted combination used as a protocol example</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','How to Store and Reconstitute Peptides Properly','','publish','open','open','','how-to-store-and-reconstitute-peptides','','','2026-04-06 03:19:56','2026-04-05 15:19:56','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/how-to-store-and-reconstitute-peptides/',0,'post','',0),(332,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:07','2026-03-12 23:13:07','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you\'re sourcing research peptides, a Certificate of Analysis is one of the most important documents you can request. Here\'s how to read one and why it matters.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is a Certificate of Analysis?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A Certificate of Analysis (COA) is a document issued by an independent laboratory that confirms the identity, purity, and quality of a specific batch of peptide. It\'s essentially proof that what\'s in the vial matches what\'s on the label.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why COAs matter</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The peptide supply chain is global and varies enormously in quality. Without independent testing, there\'s no way to verify:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Whether the peptide is actually what it claims to be</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Whether it meets the stated purity level</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Whether it contains harmful contaminants or degradation products<br>For researchers, unreliable compounds mean unreliable results. A COA removes the guesswork.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key components of a COA</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Peptide identity</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The COA should confirm the peptide\'s identity, usually through mass spectrometry (MS). This test measures the molecular weight of the compound and compares it to the expected value for that specific peptide sequence.<br><strong>What to look for:</strong> The observed molecular weight should closely match the theoretical molecular weight (within acceptable instrument tolerance).</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Purity (HPLC analysis)</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC) is the gold standard for measuring peptide purity. It separates the peptide from any impurities and calculates the percentage of the target compound in the sample.<br><strong>What to look for:</strong> Research-grade peptides should be 98% purity or higher. The HPLC chromatogram should show a single dominant peak with minimal secondary peaks.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Appearance</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A simple visual inspection confirming the peptide\'s physical form — typically described as a white to off-white lyophilised powder.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Batch/lot number</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every COA should reference a specific batch or lot number. This allows you to match the certificate to the exact product you received.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Testing date and laboratory</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The COA should identify which laboratory performed the testing and when. Third-party testing (not the manufacturer\'s own lab) provides the highest level of credibility.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Red flags to watch for</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>No batch number</strong> — the COA may not correspond to your actual product</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>In-house testing only</strong> — no independent verification</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Purity below 95%</strong> — not suitable for reliable research</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Missing mass spectrometry data</strong> — identity not confirmed</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Generic or templated COAs</strong> — may not be specific to the batch</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to request a COA from Eterna Labs</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every batch of Eterna Labs peptides is independently tested. To request a COA:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Email us with your order number and product name</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We\'ll send the relevant certificate for your specific batch</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">It\'s that simple. We believe transparency is non-negotiable.</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies third-party tested, research-grade peptides across New Zealand. Browse our range at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— used as a COA example; each batch tested to 98%+ purity</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/nad-500mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">NAD+</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a compound whose third-party COA is publicly accessible on site</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/retatrutide-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Retatrutide</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— referenced for its independent HPLC and mass spectrometry documentation</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','Understanding Certificates of Analysis (COAs)','','publish','open','open','','understanding-certificates-of-analysis','','','2026-04-06 03:19:52','2026-04-05 15:19:52','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/understanding-certificates-of-analysis/',0,'post','',0),(333,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:23','2026-03-12 23:13:23','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>CJC-1295 is one of the most popular growth hormone releasing peptides in research. But there are multiple variants — and understanding the differences matters.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is CJC-1295?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>CJC-1295 is a synthetic analogue of growth hormone releasing hormone (GHRH). It stimulates the pituitary gland to release growth hormone (GH) in a pulsatile manner, mimicking the body\'s natural rhythm.<br>There are two primary forms:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">CJC-1295 NO DAC (also called Modified GRF 1-29)</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is the shorter-acting version without the Drug Affinity Complex. It has a half-life of approximately 30 minutes and produces a brief, defined pulse of growth hormone release.<br><strong>Key characteristics:</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Shorter half-life (~30 minutes)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Produces acute GH pulses</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>More closely mimics natural GH release patterns</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Requires more frequent administration in research protocols</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">CJC-1295 WITH DAC</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The DAC (Drug Affinity Complex) modification allows the peptide to bind to albumin in the bloodstream, significantly extending its half-life to approximately 6-8 days. This creates a sustained elevation of growth hormone levels.<br><strong>Key characteristics:</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Extended half-life (~6-8 days)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Produces sustained GH elevation rather than distinct pulses</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Less frequent administration needed in research</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Higher baseline GH levels between doses</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What about Ipamorelin?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ipamorelin is a growth hormone secretagogue — it works through a different mechanism than CJC-1295. While CJC-1295 acts on the GHRH receptor, Ipamorelin acts on the ghrelin receptor (GHS-R) to stimulate GH release.<br>The key advantage of Ipamorelin in research is its selectivity. Studies suggest it promotes GH release without significantly affecting cortisol or prolactin levels, unlike some other secretagogues.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why combine CJC-1295 NO DAC + Ipamorelin?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The combination is popular in research because the two peptides work through complementary pathways:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>CJC-1295 NO DAC</strong> stimulates GH release via the GHRH pathway</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Ipamorelin</strong> amplifies the signal via the ghrelin pathway<br>Research suggests this combination may produce a synergistic effect — a greater GH response than either peptide alone. The NO DAC version is preferred for combination protocols because its shorter half-life allows for more controlled, pulsatile release patterns.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Which variant is right for your research?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:table -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>CJC-1295 NO DAC</th><th>CJC-1295 WITH DAC</th><th>CJC-1295 NO DAC + Ipamorelin</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Half-life</strong></td><td>~30 min</td><td>~6-8 days</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GH pattern</strong></td><td>Pulsatile</td><td>Sustained</td><td>Amplified pulsatile</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Frequency</strong></td><td>Higher</td><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Natural GH pattern research</td><td>Sustained GH research</td><td>Synergistic GH research</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Available at Eterna Labs</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We stock all three variants for New Zealand researchers:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"/shop/\">CJC-1295 NO DAC 10mg</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"/shop/\">CJC-1295 WITH DAC 5mg</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"/shop/\">CJC-1295 NO DAC + Ipamorelin 5mg + 5mg</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">All independently tested to 98%+ purity.</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade growth hormone peptides across New Zealand. Shop at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/cjc-1295-no-dac-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">CJC-1295 No DAC</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the short-acting variant compared directly in this article</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/cjc-1295-with-dac-5mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">CJC-1295 With DAC</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the long-acting DAC-modified variant reviewed alongside No DAC</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/cjc-1295-no-dac-ipamorelin-5mg-5mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">CJC-1295 + Ipamorelin</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the combination protocol examined as an alternative research approach</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','CJC-1295 vs CJC-1295 + Ipamorelin: What\'s the Difference?','','publish','open','open','','cjc-1295-vs-cjc-1295-ipamorelin','','','2026-04-06 03:19:48','2026-04-05 15:19:48','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/cjc-1295-vs-cjc-1295-ipamorelin/',0,'post','',0),(334,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:25','2026-03-12 23:13:25','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>NAD+ has become one of the most talked-about molecules in ageing research. Here\'s a grounded look at what scientists have found so far.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is NAD+?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (NAD+) is a coenzyme found in every living cell. It plays a central role in two critical biological processes:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Energy metabolism</strong> — NAD+ is essential for converting nutrients into cellular energy (ATP) through the mitochondria</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cellular repair</strong> — NAD+ is a substrate for enzymes like sirtuins and PARPs, which are involved in DNA repair, gene expression, and cellular stress responses<br>In short, NAD+ is fundamental to how cells produce energy and maintain themselves.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The ageing connection</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Research has consistently shown that NAD+ levels decline with age. This decline has been linked to:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Mitochondrial dysfunction</strong> — reduced energy production at the cellular level</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>DNA damage accumulation</strong> — impaired repair mechanisms</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Sirtuin activity reduction</strong> — sirtuins are a family of proteins associated with longevity, and they require NAD+ to function</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Chronic inflammation</strong> — sometimes called \"inflammageing\"<br>The hypothesis driving much of the research is straightforward: if declining NAD+ contributes to ageing processes, then restoring NAD+ levels might slow or reverse some of those processes.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key research findings</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Animal studies</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The most robust evidence comes from animal models:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Mice studies</strong> have shown that boosting NAD+ levels can improve mitochondrial function, increase energy metabolism, and extend healthspan</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Research on aged mice</strong> demonstrated improved muscle function, better insulin sensitivity, and enhanced cognitive performance after NAD+ supplementation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Sirtuin activation</strong> through NAD+ has been linked to improved DNA repair and cellular resilience in multiple preclinical studies</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Human research</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Human studies are still in earlier stages, but growing:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Several clinical trials are investigating NAD+ precursors (NMN, NR) for their effects on ageing biomarkers</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Early results suggest improvements in markers of metabolic health and cellular function</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Larger, long-term human trials are ongoing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">NAD+ in the research landscape</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>NAD+ is studied in several contexts beyond general longevity:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Neurodegenerative disease</strong> — exploring NAD+\'s neuroprotective potential</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cardiovascular health</strong> — investigating effects on vascular function and heart health</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Metabolic disorders</strong> — studying NAD+\'s role in insulin sensitivity and metabolic regulation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Exercise recovery</strong> — researching effects on mitochondrial biogenesis and muscle repair</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why researchers use NAD+ directly</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>While NAD+ precursors like NMN and NR are commonly studied, some researchers work with NAD+ itself to study direct cellular effects without relying on biosynthetic conversion pathways. This allows for more controlled investigation of NAD+-dependent processes.<br>Eterna Labs supplies <a href=\"/shop/\">NAD+ 500mg</a> for research applications, independently tested to 98%+ purity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Storage and handling</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>NAD+ should be stored:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lyophilised form:</strong> Refrigerate at 2-8°C, or freeze at -20°C for long-term storage</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Reconstituted:</strong> Refrigerate and use within 30 days</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">- <strong>Protect from light and moisture</strong> at all times</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade NAD+ across New Zealand. Browse our longevity peptides at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/nad-500mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">NAD+</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the central compound covered in this longevity research overview</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/mots-c-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">MOTS-c</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a mitochondria-derived peptide studied alongside NAD+ in ageing research</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','NAD+ and Longevity: What the Research Says','','publish','open','open','','nad-plus-and-longevity','','','2026-04-06 03:19:44','2026-04-05 15:19:44','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/nad-plus-and-longevity/',0,'post','',0),(335,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:28','2026-03-12 23:13:28','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu is one of the most extensively studied peptides in skin science. Here\'s what researchers have found and why it continues to generate interest.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is GHK-Cu?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu (glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine copper) is a naturally occurring copper peptide found in human plasma, saliva, and urine. It was first identified in the 1970s by Dr Loren Pickart, who observed that liver tissue from young donors could stimulate aged liver cells to produce proteins characteristic of younger tissue. The active factor was identified as GHK, which naturally binds to copper ions to form GHK-Cu.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why copper matters</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The copper ion in GHK-Cu isn\'t just along for the ride — it\'s functionally important. Copper is a cofactor for several enzymes involved in:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Collagen synthesis</strong> — copper-dependent lysyl oxidase is essential for collagen cross-linking</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Antioxidant defence</strong> — superoxide dismutase (SOD) requires copper to neutralise free radicals</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Wound healing</strong> — copper plays a role in angiogenesis and tissue remodelling</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu essentially serves as a delivery mechanism, bringing copper to where it\'s needed at the cellular level.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key research findings</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Collagen and extracellular matrix</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu has been shown in multiple studies to:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Stimulate collagen synthesis (types I and III)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Increase production of elastin</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Promote glycosaminoglycan (GAG) synthesis, including hyaluronic acid</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Upregulate decorin, a proteoglycan involved in collagen fibre organisation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These are the primary structural components that give skin its firmness, elasticity, and hydration.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Wound healing</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Research demonstrates GHK-Cu\'s role in wound healing through several mechanisms:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Promoting angiogenesis (new blood vessel formation)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Attracting immune cells to wound sites</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Stimulating dermal fibroblast proliferation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Reducing scar tissue formation through TGF-beta modulation</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Anti-inflammatory effects</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Studies have shown GHK-Cu can reduce inflammatory markers, including IL-6 and TNF-alpha. This is particularly relevant for skin research, as chronic low-grade inflammation is associated with accelerated skin ageing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Gene expression</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Perhaps the most interesting finding: a 2012 study by Pickart et al. found that GHK-Cu influences the expression of over 4,000 genes — roughly 6% of the human genome. Many of these genes are involved in:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>DNA repair</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Antioxidant response</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Stem cell activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Anti-inflammatory pathways</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">GHK-Cu vs other copper peptides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not all copper peptides are the same. GHK-Cu is the most studied and has the strongest body of evidence. Other copper peptides (AHK-Cu, DAHK) have different binding properties and biological activities. When reviewing the literature, it\'s important to note which specific copper peptide was used.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Research applications</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu is studied across several areas:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Skin ageing</strong> — effects on collagen, elastin, and dermal thickness</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Wound healing</strong> — acceleration of tissue repair</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Hair growth</strong> — effects on hair follicle size and cycling</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lung tissue repair</strong> — emerging research on COPD-related applications</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Anti-fibrotic effects</strong> — potential to reduce scar tissue</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Storage and handling</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>GHK-Cu should be stored:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lyophilised:</strong> 2-8°C for short-term, -20°C for long-term</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Reconstituted:</strong> Refrigerate and use within 30 days</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> The copper complex gives the reconstituted solution a characteristic blue colour — this is normal</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Eterna Labs supplies <a href=\"/shop/\">GHK-Cu 100mg</a> for research applications, independently tested to 98%+ purity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies research-grade skin and beauty peptides across New Zealand. Shop at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/ghk-cu-100mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">GHK-Cu</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— the primary compound discussed throughout this article</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/glow-70mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Glow</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">— a skin-focused peptide blend featuring GHK-Cu as a core ingredient</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>','GHK-Cu for Skin Research: A Complete Overview','','publish','open','open','','ghk-cu-for-skin-research','','','2026-04-06 03:19:40','2026-04-05 15:19:40','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/ghk-cu-for-skin-research/',0,'post','',0),(336,1,'2026-03-13 11:13:30','2026-03-12 23:13:30','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You\'ve requested a Certificate of Analysis for your peptide order: now what? Here\'s a practical guide to understanding what the numbers actually mean.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The two key tests</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most peptide purity reports include results from two primary analytical methods: HPLC and mass spectrometry. Together, they answer two fundamental questions:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Is this the right peptide?</strong> (identity)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>How pure is it?</strong> (purity)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">HPLC: Measuring purity</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What it is</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC) is a technique that separates the components of a sample based on their chemical properties. The peptide solution is pushed through a column under high pressure, and different molecules pass through at different speeds.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to read the results</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The output is a chromatogram: a graph showing peaks at different retention times. Here\'s what to look for:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Main peak:</strong> This represents your target peptide. Its area relative to the total area of all peaks gives you the purity percentage.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>98%+ purity</strong>: research grade, suitable for reliable studies</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>95-98%</strong>: acceptable for some applications but may contain interfering impurities</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Below 95%</strong>: not recommended for research where accuracy matters</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Secondary peaks:</strong> These represent impurities: incomplete synthesis products, degradation products, or contaminants. Smaller and fewer secondary peaks indicate a cleaner product.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Retention time:</strong> The time at which the main peak appears. This should be consistent with the expected value for that specific peptide.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What affects HPLC results</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Column type and conditions</strong>: different columns can give slightly different results</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Solvent gradient</strong>: the rate at which the mobile phase changes</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Detection wavelength</strong>: typically 214nm or 220nm for peptides</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mass spectrometry: Confirming identity</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What it is</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Mass spectrometry (MS) measures the molecular weight of compounds in a sample. For peptides, it confirms that the molecule has the correct mass: and therefore the correct amino acid sequence.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to read the results</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Observed mass vs theoretical mass:</strong> The report will show:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Theoretical mass</strong>: the calculated molecular weight based on the peptide\'s amino acid sequence</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Observed mass</strong>: the mass measured by the instrument</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These should match within the instrument\'s tolerance (typically within 0.1-0.5 Da for modern instruments).</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>What a mismatch means:</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>A significantly different mass suggests the wrong peptide or a synthesis error</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>A slightly higher mass might indicate adducts (additional molecules attached)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>A slightly lower mass might indicate truncation (missing amino acids)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common mass spectrometry methods</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>ESI-MS (Electrospray Ionisation)</strong>: most common for peptides</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>MALDI-TOF</strong>: useful for larger peptides and proteins</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>LC-MS</strong>: combines HPLC separation with mass spectrometry detection</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Other tests you might see</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Amino acid analysis</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Breaks the peptide down into individual amino acids and quantifies each one. Confirms the correct ratio of amino acids is present.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Endotoxin testing</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Measures bacterial endotoxin levels. Important for peptides used in sensitive research applications.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Solubility test</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Confirms the peptide dissolves properly in the recommended solvent at the expected concentration.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Appearance</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Visual description of the lyophilised product: typically \"white to off-white powder.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Putting it all together</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A good purity report should give you confidence in three things:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:table -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Test</th><th>What to look for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Is this the right peptide?</td><td>Mass spectrometry</td><td>Observed mass matches theoretical mass</td></tr><tr><td>How pure is it?</td><td>HPLC</td><td>98%+ main peak area</td></tr><tr><td>Is the batch traceable?</td><td>Lot/batch number</td><td>Unique identifier matching your product</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Eterna Labs provides</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every batch of Eterna Labs peptides is independently tested via HPLC and mass spectrometry. COAs are available on request: just email us with your order number.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We believe if a supplier can\'t show you the data, you shouldn\'t trust the product.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Eterna Labs supplies third-party tested, research-grade peptides across New Zealand. Browse our range at <a href=\"/shop/\">eternlabs.co.nz/shop</a>.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<hr style=\"margin: 2.5em 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #26262c;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #131316; border: 1px solid #26262c; padding: 24px; border-radius: 2px; margin: 2em 0;\">\n<p style=\"font-family: \'Space Grotesk\', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #01B5D8; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">Research compounds mentioned</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/bpc-157-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">BPC-157</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">: used as a purity report example throughout this article</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/retatrutide-10mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">Retatrutide</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">: one of the compounds referenced for HPLC purity benchmarking</span></li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eternapeptides.co.nz/product/ghk-cu-100mg\" style=\"color: #ffffff; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #01B5D8;\">GHK-Cu</a><span style=\"color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px;\">: a flagship peptide whose purity documentation is publicly available</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n','How to Read a Peptide Purity Report','','publish','open','open','','how-to-read-a-peptide-purity-report','','','2026-04-06 03:19:33','2026-04-05 15:19:33','',0,'https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/2026/03/13/how-to-read-a-peptide-purity-report/',0,'post','',0),(337,1,'2026-03-13 11:19:21','2026-03-12 23:19:21','<ul>\n                            <li >\n                    <a class=\'ui-e-wrap\' href=\"https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product-category/tops/\">\n                            Recovery                        \n                        <p>  </p>\n                            <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M190.5 66.9l22.2-22.2c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0L441 239c9.4 9.4 9.4 24.6 0 33.9L246.6 467.3c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.2-22.2c-9.5-9.5-9.3-25 .4-34.3L311.4 296H24c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24v-32c0-13.3 10.7-24 24-24h287.4L190.9 101.2c-9.8-9.3-10-24.8-.4-34.3z\"></path></svg>                        \n                    </a>\n                </li>\n                    </ul>\n					        <ul>\n                            <li >\n                    <a class=\'ui-e-wrap\' href=\"https://woocommerce-1174581-6265451.cloudwaysapps.com/product-category/jackets/\">\n                            Growth Hormone                        \n                        <p>  </p>\n                            <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000